    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0742" n="626" xml:id="pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100 H77/12.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 16, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The round trip will require at least six days. The road is not passable for
                    automobiles, of which indeed there are none here in proper condition; carriages
                    are uncomfortable and in bad condition. Less time would be required by coming
                    horseback, but this would be exhausting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
